From 9eab95c31a999f596e0fe788c5c8122577b5c00a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:47:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(spec-decode): profile adaptive verification on distinct
 tokens

Adaptive verification prices draft budgets from a startup profile of
dummy batches, and every dummy batch repeats token 0 (and, where the model
takes inputs_embeds, one unused embedding buffer). Identical rows route to
the same experts, so the profile barely charges for extra verification
rows, while real draft rows are distinct tokens that read more expert
weights. The resulting tables price verification far below its real cost.

With SPARK3_DSPARK_PROFILE_TOKENS=random the cost profile runs on a fixed
pseudo-random token sequence (seed 0, identical on every rank), copied by
InputBatch.make_dummy in place of zeros, and on the embeddings of those
tokens where the model takes inputs_embeds. Graph capture and every other
dummy run are unchanged; the embedding buffer is restored afterwards.
Output is unchanged.
